@@ -3542,3 +3542,42 @@ Compare PAX modification times as exact decimal nanoseconds, not rounded floats.
 Preserve a primary archive-write exception when close/footer or postguards also
 fail, recording the secondary failure separately. These guards preserve storage
 bytes and metadata; they do not establish source origin or universal quiescence.
+
+Keep historical fixture bindings keyed by path and content hash. When a live
+fixture changes, verify the old row against its original qualified config and
+immutable Git/snapshot bytes; bind the current live fixture separately.
+
+On Windows, `str(Path("/service-free/rcc"))` renders native separators even when
+a fixture starts from a POSIX-looking literal. Compare captured subprocess and
+injected-runner arguments with the same Path contract; keep version, argument
+order and timeout assertions intact. A Linux-only runtime fixture skip does not
+exclude its helper from Windows type checks. Admit callable UID/GID features
+before using POSIX ownership, read the real values once, and fail closed when
+those features are unavailable; never synthesize Windows ownership values.
+
+A managed Python executable does not establish executable search identity for
+Poetry. For a prepared Toolkit metadata guard, keep the primary pinned RCC bin
+first and its verified cached Toolkit bin second on PATH before delegation;
+check that Poetry resolves from that cached prefix. A distinct read-only probe
+can diagnose this environment without identifying an earlier discarded cause.
+Persist subprocess stdout, stderr and terminal classification before asserting
+return-code admission, on success, nonzero return, timeout and spawn failure.
+Represent unavailable streams explicitly; preserve a primary exception when
+retention also fails, and fail closed if a successful result cannot be retained.
+Use separate owned before/after captures and refuse a reused capture path.
+
+Data-only inspectors that use assertions must reject optimized Python before
+reading admission inputs; syntax compilation does not prove those checks ran.
+Require the root release to be a regular, nonsymlink, mode-0600 file before
+parsing its typed authorization. Admit all ZIP headers before reading
+payloads so a later oversized or special member cannot bypass the initial
+resource boundary. Exercise the real frozen functions against independent
+restored baselines and poisons. Structural success retains separate source,
+generated-content and consumer authority holds.
+
+Bind each Runtime distribution to its producer’s literal original checkout SHA,
+then authenticate that commit’s tree and ordered parents from retained Git API
+or Git-object evidence. A workflow’s source/head label can name the integration
+commit while the job checks out a synthetic merge; qualify each platform from
+its own original log. Producer SUCCESS and wheel-version output establish build
+identity only; inspect content and installed consumers separately.
